Contents of "cnet:" directory

    - There are four directories I use inside of the CNET directory that
      have to do with running FIDO/JamMail:

        CNet:MAIL/

            - This is by far the largest directory concerning JamMail. Look
              inside for much more information.

        CNet:PFILES/

            - There's a directory inside PFILES called FIDO. It is NOT a
              duplicate directory of the one found in MAIL. The reason I
              have one in pfiles is so I can store CNET SPECIFIC ARexx files
              dealing with FIDO and JamMail, without getting them confused
              with other types of files(Straight ARexx, DOS, etc.).

        CNet:Base1/

            - To aid in keeping LOCAL message echoes separate from my FIDO
              echoes, I created the "Base1" directory. I store all my LOCAL
              message areas in BASE0, and all my FIDO echoes in BASE1.

            - Although, at present, I only run the one network, I suggest
              creating alternate "base" directories for EACH network you
              carry, like Base2 for CLINK, Base3 for AugNet, etc...

        CNet:UDBase0/

            - Although I'm using 0, instead of 1, I suggest using the same
              technique as with the Base directories if you'll be carrying
              regular file echoes, as well as message echoes. Presently, I
              only carry the few that are required in my area, which amounts
              to four directories, so I store them in the same directory as
              my local file areas.

Dotoran
